# jsui UIs

## Shared module

- `ghq_ui_shared.js` defines `ghq_shared` (colors, `clamp`, rects, buttons, sliders, `findZone`, …).
- Both UIs: `include("ghq_ui_shared.js")`, `include("ghq_rack_map.js")`, `mgraphics.init()`, `mgraphics.relative_coords = 0`.

## State flow

- **Inbound (from `r ghq_engine_events`):** `anything()` handles `rack_state`, `control_state` (and editor also listens for `tuner_state` where drawn).
- Parse JSON into local `rackState` / per-control entries, then `mgraphics.redraw()`.
- **Outbound:** `send(...)` → `outlet(0, …)` — patch routes to engine or `open_editor` (not `messnamed` UI commands).
- Common messages: `scan`, `set_control id normalized`, `trigger_control id`, `all_off`, `open_editor` (compact only).

## Drawing

- Use `ghq_shared.colors` and existing layout; compact strip is fixed **980×176**; editor is larger (see `ghq_editor_ui.js`).
- `hitZones` rebuilt each `paint()`; `onclick` / `ondrag` use `ghq_shared.findZone`.
- Sliders throttle sends (`SLIDER_SEND_INTERVAL_MS`, `SLIDER_SEND_DELTA`) before `set_control`.

## Compact vs editor

- **Compact** (`ghq_compact_ui.js`): Utility, Amp Sims selectors, core device toggles, time/mod/reverb toggles, Scan / Off / Edit
- **Editor** (`ghq_editor_ui.js`): full rack sections, tuner display, detail sliders (`detail: true` controls in map)

## Rack map coupling

- Section layouts are partly hand-coded; new **sections** or compact shortcuts may need UI updates, not only `ghq_rack_map.js`.
- Editor can render many controls generically by section; compact only exposes a subset.

## After UI edits

- Run post-edit gate; **`node scripts/sync-user-library.js` is mandatory** so Live reloads updated `.js` from User Library.
